text:
ana_partnerships: kicking off a short thread to lock down routing + handshake rules for the upcoming marketplace + HW partner joint launch. goal = no stalled leads, clear co-sell crediting, and a reproducible ops flow. quick thoughts?

sam_sales: Thx. A few edge cases: 1) inbound marketplace leads marked as "trial" should default to hosted ops unless SI explicitly claims. 2) partners sometimes send a "fastpass" token in intro emails  do we honor that?

mike_se: Proposal: fastpass tokens are valid for 72h and guarantee immediate claim regardless of score. Otherwise we use partner_score + account_tier to route. partner_score ranges 0-100 (partner qualification).

rachel_ps: Marketing ask: we need a short co-sell blurb for the marketplace listing showing SI involvement and expected next steps. also a small badge for "SI-enabled" deals.

jordan_ops: Ops rules + infra: we'll add partner_score, fastpass_token, marketplace_listing_id, co_sell_credit_pct to the lead schema. We'll emit an event to #partner-intake when a fastpass arrives.

partner-bot: Note: upcoming marketplace freeze 2024-09-15 00:00 UTC. Any listing copy with SI references must be final by 2024-09-05.

ana_partnerships: tiny correction  my handle is ana_partnerships. Re: crediting, recommend default co_sell_credit_pct = "20%" for SI-led deals, configurable per-partner. Larger partners can have an override set in partner profile.

sam_sales: OK. Can you share routing pseudo logic? A short decision table would help AMs.

mike_se: dropping a compact table + routing pseudocode: 

```
// simplified routing logic
if (fastpass_token && token_valid(72h)) {
  route = "si-immediate";
  claim_window = 72h;
} else if (partner_score >= 70 && account_tier == "enterprise") {
  route = "si-priority";
  claim_window = 48h;
} else if (hw_tag == true && account_tier != "small") {
  route = "hw-si-first";
  claim_window = 48h;
} else if (lead_origin == "marketplace_trial") {
  route = "hosted-first";
  claim_window = 72h;
} else {
  route = "si-shared";
  claim_window = 72h;
}
```

mike_se: sample SFDC fields we will set: partner_origin, si_name, partner_score, fastpass_token, marketplace_listing_id, co_sell_credit_pct, claimed_at, claimed_by.

rachel_ps: For enablement i'll create two short templates: one email for partner-introduced leads and one for marketplace inbound. Also a 5-slide "SI co-sell play" for SI reps.

jordan_ops: webhook example (we'll JSON-POST to registered partner endpoint when claim happens): 

```
{
  "lead_id": "L-29832",
  "account_name": "BigCorp Inc.",
  "route": "si-priority",
  "claim_window_hours": 48,
  "partner_origin": "CloudVendorX",
  "si_name": "CloudVendorX SI",
  "fastpass_token": "fp-abc-2024",
  "co_sell_credit_pct": "20%"
}
```

sam_sales: Good. A couple governance items: 1) co-billing requires LOA signed before invoicing; 2) for pipeline attribution, we'll keep original partner attribution field and add marketplace_listing_id so analytics can join later.

mike_se: technical note  for hw-enabled accounts we may need a physical demo kit. ops, can we gate an automated shipping request when hw_tag == true and account_tier >= midmarket?

jordan_ops: yes, will emit fulfillment task to hw-fulfillment queue. ETA for automation: 2 weeks. will flag manual fallback in meantime.

rachel_ps: planning a joint webinar as part of the announcement push. suggested date 2024-09-18. marketing wants SI logos cleared by legal 2024-09-08.

ana_partnerships: schedule sounds fine. next actions: 
- sam_sales: compile partner overrides + credit percentages by Tue COB.
- mike_se: finalize routing decision table and share small doc for AMs by Wed.
- rachel_ps: marketing copy + 2 templates by Fri.
- jordan_ops: add partner fields to lead schema and prototype webhook by EOD Mon.

sam_sales: will start gathering overrides. quick ask  should we create a new SFDC record type for SI-introduced leads? that might help reporting.

mike_se: I'd prefer tagging over new record type to keep things simple, but if reporting needs are heavy we can revisit.

jordan_ops: tagging should be sufficient for Q3. we'll keep an eye on report fidelity.

rachel_ps: I'll loop in legal for logo clearance and PR text review.

partner-bot: Reminder: add "SI-enabled" badge to marketplace assets before 2024-09-05 to avoid relist.

ana_partnerships: thanks all. i'll create a short ops playbook and share the invite for a 30min sync on Mon 10am PT to walk through the table and webhook. please add any exceptions in this thread. :thumbsup:

mike_se: noted
